---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout title="Kindling Privacy Policy" description="How Kindling handles selected travel media, memory details, analytics, purchases, notifications, and support.">
  <article class="legal section-shell">
    <header class="legal-header">
      <p class="eyebrow">Privacy policy</p>
      <h1>Your memories deserve privacy.</h1>
      <p class="legal-notice">Effective September 16, 2026</p>
      <p>Kindling is local first and does not require an account. This policy explains what stays on your device, what can leave it, and the controls available to you.</p>
    </header>

    <nav class="legal-toc" aria-label="Privacy policy contents">
      <a href="#summary">Summary</a><a href="#local-data">Local data</a><a href="#analytics">Analytics</a><a href="#choices">Your choices</a>
    </nav>

    <section id="summary">
      <h2>1. What Kindling processes</h2>
      <div class="data-table" role="table" aria-label="Kindling data summary">
        <div role="row" class="data-row data-row--head"><span role="columnheader">Data</span><span role="columnheader">Purpose and destination</span><span role="columnheader">Retention</span></div>
        <div role="row" class="data-row"><strong role="cell">Selected media and optimized copies</strong><span role="cell">Build and display your trails on this iPhone</span><span role="cell">Until you remove the moment, trail, or app</span></div>
        <div role="row" class="data-row"><strong role="cell">Places, notes, voice memories, prompts, and tags</strong><span role="cell">App functionality and local search on this iPhone</span><span role="cell">Until you delete them</span></div>
        <div role="row" class="data-row"><strong role="cell">Product interaction analytics</strong><span role="cell">Content-free usage categories through TelemetryDeck</span><span role="cell">No more than 12 months</span></div>
        <div role="row" class="data-row"><strong role="cell">Purchase status</strong><span role="cell">Unlock and restore Kindling Pro through Apple StoreKit</span><span role="cell">Apple retains transaction records under its policies</span></div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section id="local-data">
      <h2>2. Data stored on your device</h2>
      <p>Kindling stores trip and moment structure, place labels and coordinates, your notes, private tags, prompt answers, voice recordings, import state, and sharing preferences in the app's private storage. Protected, optimized media copies keep saved trails useful even when an original is temporarily unavailable.</p>
      <p>Kindling does not operate an account or cloud synchronization service. The first memory release does not continuously scan your library, track your location, identify faces, or upload personal media for AI processing.</p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>3. Photos, microphone, maps, and sharing</h2>
      <p>The system photo picker lets you choose specific photos and videos without giving Kindling broad library access. Kindling reads available metadata from selected items to propose dates, moments, and places. Removing an item in Kindling never deletes the original from Photos.</p>
      <p>Microphone access is requested only when you tap record. Voice files stay in protected app storage. Apple map and geocoding services may receive coordinates to return map tiles or place labels under Apple's privacy terms. Network failure never prevents you from saving a trail.</p>
      <p>Sharing is user initiated. A privacy preview lets you choose whether an exported card includes the title, dates, places, notes, or sensitive moments. The system share sheet sends the finished artifact only to the destination you choose.</p>
    </section>

    <section id="analytics">
      <h2>4. Product analytics</h2>
      <p>Kindling uses TelemetryDeck for fixed events such as picker opening, import completion, Trail viewing, feature use, export success, search result-count buckets, purchase outcomes, and notification opens.</p>
      <p>Kindling does not send photos, videos, audio, filenames, coordinates, place names, trip titles, notes, tags, prompt answers, search text, persistent memory identifiers, receipts, or free-form errors to analytics. It does not use analytics for advertising, diagnosis inference, or individual profiling.</p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>5. Purchases and Apple</h2>
      <p>Apple processes Kindling Pro payments, trials, renewals, refunds, taxes, and subscription status. Kindling reads product and entitlement status through StoreKit. It does not receive your payment-card number or operate a purchase server.</p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>6. Notifications and diagnostics</h2>
      <p>Optional Postcards From Your Past use generic lock-screen text. The app checks local privacy flags before choosing a memory; sensitive, hidden, archived, deleted, and excluded moments are not eligible.</p>
      <p>Kindling does not include a third-party crash-reporting SDK. Apple may provide diagnostics if you choose to share analytics with developers in iOS Settings. Support requests are user initiated; do not email personal media or memory details unless needed for your request.</p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>7. Website and service providers</h2>
      <p>This static website does not install advertising trackers or collect memory content. Vercel may process standard request information to deliver and protect the site. Relevant providers are Apple for system services and billing, TelemetryDeck for content-free analytics, Vercel for website hosting, and your email providers when you contact support.</p>
    </section>

    <section id="choices">
      <h2>8. Export, deletion, and your choices</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Use the bundled sample without sharing any personal photos.</li>
        <li>Decline microphone or notification permission without losing the core Trail.</li>
        <li>Hide a moment, mark it sensitive, or prevent resurfacing.</li>
        <li>Export your memory text and structure as JSON from Settings.</li>
        <li>Delete one trail or all Kindling data without contacting support.</li>
        <li>Clear disposable previews and exports without deleting memories.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>Deleting the app removes its current local data from the iPhone. Apple device backups may retain an earlier encrypted copy under Apple's backup controls.</p>
    </section>

    <section><h2>9. Children, changes, and contact</h2><p>Kindling is not directed to children under 13. We may update this policy when the product or law changes and will post a revised effective date. Questions can be sent to <a href="mailto:hello@maskedsyntax.com">hello@maskedsyntax.com</a>.</p></section>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
